'' docs/tiko-properties R12, RUN: A PROPERTY PASSED BYREF IS COPIED BACK -- get into a temporary,
'' call, set from it, as VB.NET and Swift do (decision Q5: R12c). fbc passes the temporary and
'' loses the write. Over an indexed property, a static one, a namespace's double, a method's
'' parameter, a string, a function in an expression and a register-sized UDT. Not copied back:
'' a 'byref as const' parameter, an init-only auto-property, and a private setter from outside its
'' type -- each stays a temporary. tiko-only behaviour, so each line was checked by hand.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/propbyref.tiko -o tests/codegen/propbyref.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/propbyref.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: show 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  6 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  100
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  6 a!
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  12 12
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1
